<section class="about-section">
  <h1>about</h1>
  <p>Lucid Vagary is a home for image-poems and poetry — where creativity inspires insight.</p>
  <p>The site gathers drawings, sketches, photographs, and writing made over many years, presenting them together so each work can be read alongside the others.</p>
  <h2>Finding your way</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/collection/">Collections</a> bring works together through deliberate groupings.</li>
    <li><a href="/constellations/">Constellations</a> trace connections that cross those groupings.</li>
    <li>The <a href="/archive/">archive</a> lists every artwork and piece of writing, with filters by type, subject, and year.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>About the work</h2>
  <p>The work at Lucid Vagary moves between image and language. Image-poems pair a poem with a photograph or drawing so that each reads through the other.</p>
  <p>Drawings and sketches explore eyes, faces, masks, hands, and inner landscapes, often recurring across years and series such as <a href="/posts/The-Pentaptych-of-Growth/">The Pentaptych of Growth</a>.</p>
  <p>See a selection of <a href="/sketchbook/">sketchbook pages</a>.</p>
  <p>Some pieces carry personal histories; <a href="/posts/the-city/">The City on the Lake</a>, for example, was written at the site of the author's hemorrhagic stroke.</p>
</section>
